## Syntax Summary: message-commands vs. Mode Indicators

### message-command Syntax (From Tyler to 1000xdev)

- **Basic Format**: `message-command: standard-parameter @project-rule-parameter.mdc`
- **Characteristics**:
  - Always lowercase
  - Always kebab-case (words separated by hyphens)
  - Always includes a colon before parameters
  - Never includes brackets around parameters

### Mode Indicator Syntax (From 1000xdev to Tyler)

- **Basic Format**: `emoji 1000xdev [workflow-type]`
- **Characteristics**:
  - Always begins with emoji (📋 for plan-mode, 💻 for dev-mode)
  - Always includes "1000xdev"
  - Always includes workflow type in square brackets

### Key Syntax Distinctions

| Feature | message-commands (Tyler) | Mode Indicators (1000xdev) |
|---|-----|----|
| Case | lowercase only | Mixed case with emoji |
| Colons | Required before parameters | Never used |
| Brackets | Never used | Required around workflow-type |
| Format | message-command: standard-parameter @message-command.mdc | emoji 1000xdev [workflow-type] |
| Example | plan-mode: rules-workflow @plan-mode.mdc | 📋 1000xdev [rules-workflow] |
| Example | dev-mode: rules-workflow @dev-mode.mdc | 💻 1000xdev [rules-workflow] |
| Example | direct-mode: rules-workflow @direct-mode.mdc | ⚡ 1000xdev [rules-workflow] |

